-- title:
--   Frobenius pull-back annihilates ℓ-torsion in Pic⁰ mod ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, let $\ell$ be a prime and assume $K$ has characteristic $\ell$, and let $N$ be a nonzero natural number. Write $\bar F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC K N` for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by the family `divisorExpansionsC K N` of $q$-expansions, and let `JZeroC K N` be its degree-zero divisor class group, i.e. the quotient of the group of degree-zero divisors of $\bar F/K$ by the subgroup of principal divisors lying in it. The endomorphism `frobeniusPullbackModL K N ℓ` of this group is defined by cases: if the conjunction `FrobeniusInputsModL K N ℓ` holds — namely that $\bar F/K$ has principal divisors, that `frobeniusModL K N ℓ` is finite along, and that the fundamental identity and the norm formula hold along it — it is the map induced on classes by pull-back of degree-zero divisors along `frobeniusModL K N ℓ`, and otherwise it is the zero homomorphism. The assertion is that for every $x$ in `JZeroC K N` with $(\ell : \mathbb{Z}) \cdot x = 0$ one has `frobeniusPullbackModL K N ℓ x = 0`; that is, the Frobenius pull-back kills the $\ell$-torsion of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(\bar F/K)$.
--
--   Classically this is the statement that $\mathrm{Fr}^* = [\ell]\circ\sigma^{-1}$ vanishes on $\ell$-torsion of the Jacobian in characteristic $\ell$, so that the Eichler–Shimura relation $\bar T_\ell = \mathrm{Fr}_* + \mathrm{Fr}^*$ reduces on $\mathrm{Pic}^0[\ell]$ to the Frobenius push-forward alone. It is used for exactly that reduction and in the subsequent analysis of the Hecke action on the $\ell$-torsion of the Jacobian of the modular curve in characteristic $\ell$.
